s of the census of 2000, there were 2,104 people, 787 households, and 497 families residing in the city. The population density was 1,277.3 per square mile (492.3/km²). There were\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0219-84eaf5487f69:d01\", \"text\": \"Marlette Township, Michigan Marlette Township is a civil township of Sanilac County in the U.S. state of Michigan. The population was 2,051 at the 2000 census. According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of , all land. As of the census of 2000, there were 2,051 people, 697 households, and 579 families residing in the township. The population density was 39.1 per square mile (15.1/km²). There were 743 housing units at an average density of 14.2 per square mile (5.5/km²). The racial makeup of the township was 97.90% White, 0.15% African American, 0.20% Native\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0219-84eaf5487f69:d02\", \"text\": \") , all land . Demographics [ edit ] Historical population Census Pop . Note % ± 2000 2,051 — 2010 1,763 −14.0 % 2020 1,686 −4.4 % As of the census [ 1 ] of 2000 , there were 2,051 people , 697 households , and 579 families residing in the township . The population density was 39.1 inhabitants per square mile ( 15.1/km 2 ) . There were 743 housing units at an average density of 14.2 per square mile ( 5.5/km 2 ) . The racial makeup of the township was 97.90 % White , 0.15 %\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"The population of Marlette is not specified without additional context, as there are multiple places named Marlette.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0219-84eaf5487f69:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0219-84eaf5487f69:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Marlette\", \"scope\": \"As of the census of 2000\", \"claim\": \"As of the census of 2000, the population of Marlette was 2,104.\", \"answer\": \"2,104\", \"quote\": \"As of the census of 2000, there were 2,104 people, 787 households, and 497 families residing in the city.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}